From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:29:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] build: use tsrs for Node executor checks and expose CLI
 selection

Run the Node executor no-emit check with pinned tsrs and bundler resolution while retaining esbuild for both CommonJS runtime bundles. Track its tsconfig as a Cargo input and preserve unrelated workspace dependency resolutions.

Mirror the standalone CLI tsrs selector, extended-version parsing and file-observation protocol. Older tsc-based clients remain compatible without a backend protocol change. Keep SDK declarations, ES5 system UDFs and the runtime browser-interface type baseline on their existing compilers.

Document supported build hosts and the exact-release installation exception. Preserve the global dependency release-age policy.
