 </Admonition>
 
+To use `tsrs`, install the `tsrs` package in your project and set
+`"typescriptCompiler": "tsrs"` in `convex.json`. This selects it for
+development, deployment, and code-generation typechecks. For one check,
+`convex typecheck --typescript-compiler tsrs` overrides the project setting.
+Convex does not substitute `tsc` if the selected compiler is missing; the
+existing `--typecheck` enable, try, and disable modes still apply.
+
+tsrs 0.18 uses TypeScript 7.1 development semantics and supports Linux x64/arm64
+and macOS arm64. Review your project's TypeScript configuration and diagnostics
+when switching compilers. Compiler selection does not change JavaScript bundling
+or the SDK's declaration build.
+
